&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll become part of the Trust’s Detection team, with a mission to protect the Vinted community from harmful activities and content. The Detection team in the Trust domain is engaged in detecting, understanding, and stopping illegal, dangerous or inappropriate content within the Vinted Marketplace. As a Decision Scientist embedded in a product team, you will become part of a cross-functional team and drive quality decisions by bringing actionable insights from data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead hypothesis-driven product experimentation, translating data into actionable insights and product improvements. You will design and evaluate experiments with support from experienced stakeholders, ensuring rigorous validation of results and a clear, measurable impact, while maintaining high standards of data quality and accessibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;As a Decision Scientist at Vinted, you’ll:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with your team and stakeholders to identify strategic opportunities and provide data-driven recommendations and answer critical business questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside other decision scientists to detect and investigate specific fraud patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test and analyse opportunities to validate their value and understand their business impact, using statistical methods and visualisation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select, calculate, and monitor your team&#39;s key performance indicators, proactively flagging issues, running analyses, and understanding root causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable your team and direct stakeholders to independently leverage data for business insights via self-service dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a data-driven culture by promoting best practices in analytics and decision-making to make data count.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a Decision Science or Data Analytics role (3+ years).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good analytical thinking and problem-solving skills, with the ability to balance depth of analysis with business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SQL and Python for data analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with BI tools (e.g., Looker, Tableau, Power BI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of statistical methods, such as A/B testing, regression analysis, and other inferential techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly results-oriented and comfortable with iterative processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator who can convincingly present results to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English, both written and spoken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advantage: experience working in the Trust &amp;amp; Safety or Fraud-related area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advantage: previous experience working in product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work perks&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to benefit from our share options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 days of paid annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Newest MacBook models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office support: we provide IT workstation equipment and a personal budget of up to €540 for home workplace furniture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lunch benefit per your workday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent team-building events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A personal monthly budget for shopping on Vinted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a discounted gym membership plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension Plan with Vinted matching 150% of your chosen contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supplemental Private Health Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life and Disability insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A subsidised Deutschlandticket for your commute to the office by public transport&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dog-friendly office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workation policy [[DELETE IF NOT RELEVANT]]&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Better balance holidays with workdays by working remotely! Up to 90 days per year in the EU, of these, 21 days can be spent globally. For non-EU citizens, it&#39;s 21 days worldwide. This can be combined with time off for vacation or personal time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each year, you’ll be given a learning budget (starting at €3,000), and a total of up to 10 working days over a 2-year period to support your personal and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid work&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our hybrid model, with 2 recommended office days a week, gives you and your team the flexibility to decide if and when you want to work from home, and when to catch up in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from everybody, regardless of your background, identity, or life experiences. Job openings come with guides, not checklists. If you’re excited about a role, but don’t identify with every point in the ‘About you’ section, apply anyway – you might still be the perfect match!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual gross salary range for this position is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€74.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€100.100 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2017, Wayve is the leading developer of Embodied AI technology.&amp;nbsp; Our advanced AI software and foundation models enable vehicles to perceive, understand, and navigate any complex environment, enhancing the usability and safety of automated driving systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is to create autonomy that propels the world forward.&amp;nbsp; Our intelligent, mapless, and hardware-agnostic AI products are designed for automakers, accelerating the transition from assisted to automated driving.&amp;nbsp; &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In our fast-paced environment big problems ignite us—we embrace uncertainty, leaning into complex challenges to unlock groundbreaking solutions. We aim high and stay humble in our pursuit of excellence, constantly learning and evolving as we pave the way for a smarter, safer future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Wayve, your contributions matter.&amp;nbsp; We value diversity, embrace new perspectives, and foster an inclusive work environment; we back each other to deliver impact.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Make Wayve the experience that defines your career!&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re passionate about quality and continuous improvement, this role offers the opportunity to ensure the effectiveness of training programs, materials and delivery methods, while working closely with teams to uphold operating standards and support professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and evaluate the effectiveness of training programs and make recommendations for improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain training records and ensure compliance with company policies and legal requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular assessments of operating standards across teams and individuals to ensure they meet quality standards and objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain training materials, including manuals, presentations, and online resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with subject matter experts to identify areas for improvement in training content, delivery and operating standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyse training metrics to identify trends and opportunities for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and oversee the implementation of quality assurance processes for training programs and operating standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In conjunction with Team Leads, assist with staff professional development and course completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interact with cross-functional stakeholders to understand training requirements for future business needs e.g. growth of commercial operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In order to set you up for success as a Trainer at Wayve, we’re looking for the following skills and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essentials:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full clean DE driving licence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 8 years&#39; driving experience - mainly in DE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No blameworthy insurance claims in the past three years.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You remain calm and controlled in a pressured environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take on board feedback and learn from your mistakes, employing a growth mindset to the way you develop yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working with people, thriving in a team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know how to manage your wellbeing including fatigue, stress and have personal, proven strategies to do this&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a team coordinator or similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership and communication skills in a 1:1 capacity, downwards to your team, and upwards and laterally with your other stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work under pressure and manage multiple priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Workspace or Microsoft Office suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent time management and organisational skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A recognised Assessor qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A qualified Vehicle Safety Operator with a current qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A recognised Quality Assurance qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available to work full-time on-site based out of our Leonberg office, 5 days a week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All applications are required to disclose any second job as part of the application process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All applications will be subject to a health check before/after.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employment is contingent upon passing training, pre-employment checks and ongoing drug/alcohol testing, in accordance with our policy. You will be tested for drugs and alcohol during your onsite interview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-KM2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Wayve is committed to creating an inclusive interview experience. If you require any accommodations or adjustments to participate fully in our interview process, please let us know.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We understand that everyone has a unique set of skills and experiences and that not everyone will meet all of the requirements listed above. If you’re passionate about self-driving cars and think you have what it takes to make a positive impact on the world, we encourage you to apply.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Wayve we&#39;re committed to creating a diverse, fair and respectful culture that is inclusive of everyone based on their unique skills and perspectives, and regardless of sex, race, religion or belief, ethnic or national origin, disability, age, citizenship, marital, domestic or civil partnership status, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy or related condition&amp;nbsp; (including breastfeeding) or any other basis as protected by applicable law. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://wayve.ai/careers/&quot;&gt;Careers at Wayve.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about what drives us, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://wayve.ai/careers/&quot;&gt;Values at Wayve&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US candidates only, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N46n3iN0AG8EPEO-hCanyyv7hzz8KgT_/view?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;E-Verify Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ussc.gov/sites/default/files/pdf/employment/RightToWork.pdf&quot;&gt;Participation and Right to Work&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DISCLAIMER: We will not ask about marriage or pregnancy, care responsibilities or disabilities in any of our job adverts or interviews. However, we do look to capture information about care responsibilities, and disabilities among other diversity information as part of an optional DEI Monitoring form to help us identify areas of improvement in our hiring process and ensure that the process is inclusive and non-discriminatory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Waymo Safety team works to promote and help to continuously improve the safety of Waymo’s fully autonomous driving technology. Our experts develop safety goals and strategies, and conduct safety engineering analyses to ensure safety is being considered throughout the design and development of our vehicles. The team develops and promotes safety strategies and policies for autonomous vehicles for its work with regulatory authorities, lawmakers, law enforcement and public and non-profit organizations. Our Safety Team also helps advise on compliance with applicable environmental, health, and safety regulations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Emergency Services Liaison - Outreach Teams are integral to ensuring that in any Waymo market, local responders have a good working knowledge of the vehicles and in-built technology, and also have the confidence to safely and effectively interact with the vehicles and riders at any operational incident.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In this role you will be hybrid based in Munich and report into our Head of Enterprise Resilience&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive strategic engagement and cultivate long-term trust with German emergency services by positioning Waymo as a transparent, collaborative partner committed to their safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the recruitment and training of Emergency Services Ambassadors (ESAs) to serve as local advocates, acting as the definitive subject matter expert for all responder-related inquiries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spearhead the implementation and continuous improvement of Waymo’s German Emergency Services Familiarization Program by benchmarking global best practices and ensuring responders remain confident in their ability to interact safely with Waymo technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the voice of Waymo at industry events and panels, influencing by bridging the gap between Emergency Services and AV technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect robust Emergency Services communication that captures and channels critical feedback directly into our engineering teams, driving continuous product improvements around Emergency Services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate internal alignment by translating responder insights into actionable strategic improvements, ensuring our engineering and operations teams are always responsive to the evolving realities of Emergency Services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of service in German emergency services (Polizei, Feuerwehr, or Rettungsdienst)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of German legal frameworks (Datenschutz/GDPR, Rettungskette), emergency protocols, and community engagement strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in emergency response and building relationships with Emergency Services organisations such as the Berliner Feuerwehr and Polizei Berlin, along with a&amp;nbsp; strong understanding of the specific nuances and sensitivities of Emergency Services communities&amp;nbsp; in Germany.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and presentation skills, in both German and English, capable of engaging diverse audiences, combined with an ability&amp;nbsp; to lead, motivate and develop teams, constantly striving for excellence across all areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative mindset and the ability to work effectively with legal and other internal teams, combined with experience of being able to&amp;nbsp; stay focused and deliver under competing pressures, whilst ensuring that programs remain on track and deadline targets are consistently met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 7 years in a leadership or management position within one of Germany&#39;s principal emergency services, with a proven record of collaborative&amp;nbsp; inter-agency working, and the ability to engage with strategic, tactical and operational teams as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing organisational presence in new geographic locations, operating in rapidly scaling and complex operational environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with autonomous vehicle technology and its implications for emergency services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of policy development related to emergency management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a role requiring significant public speaking and stakeholder engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;~20% travel (Domestic &amp;amp; International)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred locations are Frankfurt,&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Berlin,&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Munich or Hanover; with domestic and occasional international travel as required.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As demand for high-performance, cross-border connectivity continues to grow, euNetworks expands its European presence. We are seeking a dynamic and commercially driven Account Director to join our European team in France or in Belgium, focusing on wholesale carriers and telecom resellers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact, customer-facing role responsible for both account management and new business development within the wholesale market. You’ll represent one of Europe’s most advanced fibre networks, delivering scalable, low-latency connectivity solutions across key routes and data centre hubs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work closely with some of the most established names and fastest-growing players in the telecom sector, helping them access and resell high-capacity infrastructure services throughout Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will you be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and grow strategic relationships with wholesale carriers and telecom resellers across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and win new business opportunities, positioning euNetworks’ long-haul and metro fibre services to support customer growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage existing accounts, ensuring strong customer satisfaction, revenue retention, and opportunity development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position our European network solutions — including high-capacity, low-latency routes and unique data centre connectivity offerings — to meet evolving customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with internal teams including Pre-Sales, Product, and Network Development to deliver tailored solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and manage pipeline activity using Salesforce.com, ensuring accurate forecasting and data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend and represent euNetworks at relevant industry events and forums across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do we want from you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in Sales or Pre-sales (at least 8 years) preferably with wholesale carriers or with Service integrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of the telecoms market, particularly within the carrier and reseller ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of growing accounts and securing new logos in a competitive landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand and position technical network solutions (e.g. wavelengths, dark fibre, Ethernet, IP transit) to a commercially savvy audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in German and English, with effective communication and presentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter mindset — proactive, results-driven, and comfortable working in a fast-moving, cross-border environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this position is of interest but you don’t think you meet all of the criteria listed, please consider applying still. euNetworks looks to recruit people with the right attitude, potential and ambition and for the right candidate, we will provide further training and support to enable you to develop in the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What can we offer you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At euNetworks we invest in our people by offering a range of benefits and development opportunities designed to support your professional growth and personal wellbeing. Employees have access to a comprehensive wellbeing programme that promotes mental health and also recognises the importance of work-life balance through initiatives such as a dedicated birthday day off and “give back” days to support volunteering activities. euNetworks’ bonus scheme is linked to both individual contribution and overall company performance with opportunity to overachieve in both areas. In addition, euNetworks operates a flexible hybrid working policy, enabling employees to balance in-office collaboration with remote work, fostering productivity, autonomy and a positive employee experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Family Friendly Policy delivers enhanced and inclusive parental benefits that can viewed &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1yM2VvLsByNiULKnRX9pIksCK0GI6FmO2/edit?usp=sharing&amp;amp;ouid=105588911760161167743&amp;amp;rtpof=true&amp;amp;sd=true&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Insurances, pensions, leave and additional enhancements are modelled to work with local country provisions, please email &lt;a ---------- for more details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our company values drive our behaviour and form the basis of how we operate our business. We work as a team promoting a culture of collaboration, trust and respect where every individual is heard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and commit to providing each individual with the support, continued learning and the tools to achieve their goals and an environment in which they can thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to make the hiring process equitable and accessible for all. Providing candidates with the opportunity to be their true selves and explore how you might thrive at euNetworks. We are a recognised Disability Confident employer and will make provisions where possible to support you through the interview process, if you require any reasonable accommodation through the selection process, please let your Talent Partner know.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At OpenUp, our mission is to make mental well-being accessible to everyone. Following a ‘high tech &amp;amp; high touch’ approach, we support companies, their employees, and their families with proactive and practical mental health services. Through our digital platform, clients can access 1:1 check-ins, online courses, articles, videos, group sessions, mindfulness practices, and a team of committed mental well-being experts. As we believe that mental and physical well-being are deeply connected, we have also added Lifestyle Experts to our offering, focusing on nutrition, exercise, and sleep. We offer a truly holistic approach that helps people take ownership of their health. We’re proud to work with forward-thinking organizations and are committed to raising the bar on accessible care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OpenUp was ranked in the Top 3 on LinkedIn’s Top Startups list for 2023, 2024 &amp;amp; 2025 and is continuously growing. We are expanding our international teams and we are searching for like-minded talent. We are already serving 2000+ companies (e.g. Rituals, Deloitte, Decathlon, KPMG, and McDonalds), through which 600K+ employees have access to our product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building out our presence in the DACH market and are looking for an entrepreneurial, purpose driven Sales Director to lead this market with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you take full ownership of our commercial success in DACH. You coach and develop our Account Executives, shape our go to market strategy, and act as our trusted advisor on the German market for the wider organisation. This is not a &quot;manage and report&quot; role; it&#39;s an opportunity to build a market from the ground up and lead from the front, including closing deals yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with our Business Development, Customer Success, and Marketing teams as part of a collaborative, international commercial team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the go to market strategy for the DACH region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, develop, and grow a team of Account Executives (currently scaling from 2 to 6)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and expand the market, including new B2B partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the internal advisor and voice of the German market for our (Dutch) headquarters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take full ownership of the DACH sales function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close deals yourself, staying hands on and close to the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You genuinely enjoy working with people; you&#39;re energised by conversations, coaching your team, and building relationships at different levels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You bring a combination of drive, curiosity, and resilience. You take ownership, learn from setbacks, and continuously look for ways to improve. You&#39;re comfortable operating in a fast paced, still to be built environment and enjoy being part of a team that builds together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mental well being resonates with you as something that matters and something you want to contribute to.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of leadership experience in B2B SaaS or tech sales, ideally within HR SaaS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine hunter mentality and a strong instinct for go to market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling a market or sales team from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm for staying personally involved in closing deals, not just leading from behind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of the German market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ambition paired with a warm, human way of leading people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you can expect&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining OpenUp means being part of a fast-growing company that&#39;s doing something meaningful. You&#39;ll work with a diverse and international team. We like to have fun together with a lot of team building activities like our weekly ‘borrels’ and after work sport classes, the yearly ski-trip and our Padel tournament. Which makes our work fun, challenging and dynamic. Apart from this, we offer:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;€1500 annual personal development budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ClassPass: OpenUp contributes towards your classpass membership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly home internet/phone contribution (50EUR)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily healthy and vegetarian lunch at our Amsterdam office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular office yoga, meditation classes or breathing exercises (at our Amsterdam office)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work model (hybrid and options for remote work).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly drinks and company wide summer fest and other fun activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;27.5 vacation days per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free and unlimited access for you and your family to all our products, including our psychologists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inspired to be part of OpenUp? We’d love to hear your story. Apply via our website and we’ll get in touch soon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have questions, please visit our &lt;a href=&quot;https://openup.com/nl/veelgestelde-vragen/&quot;&gt;FAQ page&lt;/a&gt; or reach out directly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At OpenUp, everyone is welcome to apply regardless of age, gender, background, nationality, or any other characteristic. What matters to us is high performance, a real drive to make an impact and the ambition to become the European market leader. If you&#39;re ready to OpenUp, join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to streamline parts of our recruitment process. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgement. All hiring decisions are made by humans. If you would like more information about how we use AI in the process, please contact us.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;At OpenUp, we believe mental well-being should be as accessible and normal as going to the gym. Our mission is simple but ambitious: to make mental well-being available to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;We partner with companies to support their employees and families through proactive, practical mental health services. Our platform brings together 1:1 check-ins, courses, content, group sessions, and mindfulness practices - all supported by a dedicated network of experts. We take a holistic view, connecting mental and physical well-being through lifestyle coaching focused on sleep, nutrition, and exercise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, we support over 1,500 companies and 500,000+ employees globally, including Rituals, Deloitte, Decathlon, KPMG, and McDonald’s. Recognised as a Top 3 LinkedIn Startup in 2023, 2024 and 2025 - and we&#39;ve got big plans to keep growing our client-base, which is where this role comes into play.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;We’re growing our presence in the DACH market and are looking for entrepreneurial, purpose-driven Account Executives to help build this market with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;In this role, you own the full sales cycle end-to-end - from identifying opportunities and opening conversations, through to closing deals and building long-term relationships. This is not a “plug-and-play” sales role; it’s an opportunity to shape how we grow in DACH.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You’ll work closely with our Business Development, Customer Success, and Marketing teams as part of a collaborative, international commercial team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new business by identifying and engaging potential clients across the DACH region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and expand a strong network of B2B partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow existing accounts by spotting expansion opportunities (including international rollouts)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted first point of contact for your customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What you&#39;ll bring to our team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You genuinely enjoy working with people; you’re energised by conversations, building relationships, and connecting with stakeholders at different levels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You bring a combination of drive, curiosity, and resilience. You take ownership, learn from setbacks, and continuously look for ways to improve. You’re comfortable operating in a fast-paced environment and enjoy being part of a team that builds together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Mental well-being resonates with you as something that matters and something you want to contribute to.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in sales (ideally B2B SaaS or high-growth environments)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationship-building skills - you’re a natural, confident and engaging networker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience - or interest - in building a network within HR or People teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in closing deals with medium- to large-enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A structured, action-oriented way of working and a relationship-focussed sales approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm for working in a highly dynamic, AI-forward international environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with tools like Salesforce, HubSpot, or Pipedrive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent language skills in both German and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll get as part of our team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You’ll join a company that combines commercial ambition with meaningful impact. We move fast, support each other, and make time to celebrate along the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Alongside a competitive salary and bonus structure, we offer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;€1500 annual personal development budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribution to your ClassPass membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;€50 monthly internet/phone allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily healthy, vegetarian lunch at the office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular yoga, meditation, and breathing sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible hybrid working model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly drinks, summer events, ski trips, and padel tournaments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;27.5 vacation days per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free and unlimited access to OpenUp for you and your family, including sessions with psychologists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next steps:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inspired to be part of OpenUp? We’d love to hear your story. Apply via our website and we’ll get in touch soon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have questions, please visit our &lt;a href=&quot;https://openup.com/nl/veelgestelde-vragen/&quot;&gt;FAQ page&lt;/a&gt; or reach out directly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At OpenUp, everyone is welcome to apply regardless of age, gender, background, nationality, or any other characteristic. What matters to us is high performance, a real drive to make an impact and the ambition to become the European market leader. If you&#39;re ready to OpenUp, join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to streamline parts of our recruitment process. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgement. All hiring decisions are made by humans. If you would like more information about how we use AI in the process, please contact us.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Brief&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a buyer responsible for organizing the transports, you will drive the efficient and reliable movement of goods and materials across national and international locations, ensuring seamless logistics operations within our supply chain. You will collaborate with internal stakeholders and external partners to schedule transportation, negotiate contracts, manage documentation, and uphold compliance with industry standards. Your proactive approach to optimizing costs, tracking performance, and maintaining deadlines will directly support our mission to deliver high-quality aerospace products, on time and on budget.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Role in Our Space Mission:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, direct, and coordinate the transportation, storage, and distribution of goods and services, both nationally and internationally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule timely transportation services and monitor shipments to ensure goods reach their destinations as planned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select appropriate means of transport and arrange logistics with nominated carriers, brokers, and freight forwarders for land, sea, and air freight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain and negotiate contract terms with drivers and other vendors to secure favorable agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate, process, and administer detailed transportation documents and invoices, ensuring all documentation is accurately completed, properly stored, and maintained for full traceability and audit purposes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track transportation budgets and expenses, maintaining cost targets and performance control of service providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement, and maintain transportation policies and procedures, ensuring compliance with industry regulations, plant standards, and shipping requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish priorities, track assignments, and ensure availability of resources needed for efficient operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain schedules and deadlines for all transport activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively with loading and warehouse personnel to meet shipment goals and optimize logistics processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification Checklist&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Supply Chain Management, Logistics, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in transport organization, logistics, or freight purchasing (national and international)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of transportation regulations and industry standards (land, sea, and air freight)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with contract negotiation and vendor management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid knowledge of customs procedures, exim (export/import) processes, export control regulations, and handling of dangerous goods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational and multitasking skills, with the ability to prioritize and meet deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset with strong attention to detail and cost optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication skills in English (written and spoken);&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively with internal teams and external partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solving skills and a proactive, solution-oriented approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonus Skills&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in using logistics and ERP systems (e.g., SAP) would be a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
